fran: quick convo: compact-left-rail prototype highlights a deeplink mismatch. pasted an example in figma.

fran: reproduction: /org/zephyr/ws/omega/insights/metrics/42 opens rail but highlights 'Insights' group rather than the 'MRR metrics' child. url is correct.

kevin: saw that. behavior comes from our match strategy being prefix-first. child routes exist but never win.

yara: proposal: adjust resolver precedence. order: 1) literal fullPath, 2) paramized pattern match (use route patterns), 3) legacy alias map, 4) prefix fallback. this makes the specific child route authoritative.

oscar: agree. important: when resolved != requested, canonicalize the address bar but keep back-button friendly behavior. i suggest push(orig) then replace(resolved) so external referrers still go back to mail. pseudocode:
```
const req = normalize(location.href);
const resolved = resolve(req);
if (resolved !== req) {
  history.pushState({orig: req}, '', req);
  history.replaceState({}, '', resolved);
  showTinyBanner('Showing closest match — Open original', {href: req});
} else {
  history.replaceState({}, '', resolved);
}
```

kevin: banner should be subtle and session-dismissible. copy options: 'Showing closest match' vs 'We opened the nearest page'. prefer concise.

yara: accessibility: move focus to the resolved item link and set aria-current="page" there. if group needed expansion, set aria-expanded="true" on the group toggle and announce via a polite live region: 'Group expanded: Insights. MRR metrics selected.' ensure live region fires after focus change.

oscar: dev Q: where to store aliasMap? prefer nav-manifest in ui repo (source-controlled) with a small runtime patch api. keeps changes auditable.

fran: normalizer notes: strip hash anchors, drop trailing slash, decode, lowercase non-id segments, stable-sort query keys except tokens. also map #section -> ?anchor= for analytics.

kevin: keyboard detail: when user presses shortcut to focus nav, focus should land on highlighted resolved child. if child was revealed by expansion, animate a quick fade for the highlight to reduce jump. respect prefers-reduced-motion.

yara: unit tests: slug collision (group slug == item id), trailing slash/hash normalization, canonicalization push/replace/pop flows, banner show/hide logic. add telemetry when collisions occur.

oscar: analytics: emit event {from:req, to:resolved, banner_shown, banner_clicked}. track clicks to decide whether to create permanent redirects.

nav-helper: preview link: https://preview.redwood/nav/compact-deeplink-2209 (ephemeral)

fran: action items: @kevin update resolver PR to exact->param->alias->prefix + add collision tests; @yara paste ARIA snippets in the PR; @oscar prototype push+replace flow and demo popstate behavior; fran will upload compact vs resolved highlight mock to figma. sync tomorrow 10am.

kevin: on it. adding unit tests now.

yara: i'll paste the a11y snippets after lunch.

oscar: demo incoming later today :thumbsup:
